WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.380
STEPHANIE WONG: We're talking
about Kubernetes, reCAPTCHA,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.530
and AppSheet.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.170
I'm Stephanie Wong, and
welcome to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.090
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.850
news from the safety of home.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.060
Working with Kubernetes often
means working with YAML,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.860
and custom resource
definitions can

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.020
introduce even more complexity.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.520
That's why we wanted
to let you know

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.410
about Cloud Code's expanded
support for Kubernetes CRDs.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.990
Cloud Code supports IDEs
and helps you write, run,

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.360
and debug cloud-native
applications,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.660
and now also supports inline
documentation, completions,

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.800
and linting for both
popular and custom CRDs.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.090
Web traffic is at a record high,
but for more than just humans.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.770
Traffic from automated
systems is also on the rise.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.160
And while not all
bots are malicious,

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.890
you can keep your business
secure with reCAPTCHA

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.120
Enterprise.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.360
Enterprise introduces better
security, risk analysis,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.900
and abuse protection without
making your users select which

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.820
squares contain a stoplight.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.370
See how it works, and
keep your system secure.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.820
Google Workspace is all about
collaboration and staying

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.830
productive.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.970
AppSheet lets you take
that one step further

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.910
by letting you build
no-code custom apps,

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.910
or you can use Apps Script
to extend and modify

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.260
with some quick code.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.058
Use either or both to
do more, and if you're

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.850
looking for how to get
started, take a look

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.070
at the solutions gallery
for some examples.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.070
Finally, thanks for
sticking with us as we

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.590
brought you the lowest latency
news from the safety of home.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:33.310
It's been a fun challenge making
our content from our own homes,

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.970
so we're giving the team
a well-deserved break.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.180
This is the last episode of the
year, and This Week in Cloud

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.955
will be back in 2021.

00:01:40.955 --> 00:01:43.080
If you want to read more
about these announcements,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.330
check out the link in
the video description.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.150
And feel free to continue
sharing your thoughts and ideas

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.320
by commenting or tweeting us.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.950
We'll see you in the Cloud.

